            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>At the time of the inspection we notice some air leakage on the following house components:

-Windows: All wood units

-Doors (Basement back door)

-Receptacles

-Woodstove chimney

The re-insulation of the exterior walls will increase the airtightness of the building and the installation of weather stripping to seal the doors will reduce air leakage. 

</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-19. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square inch for the addition of R-20+, and $ 3.50/square inch for R-30+. The insulation will help you to increase the airtightness of your home and contribute to energy savings.</mainWalls>
                <foundation>The basement wall is composed of a 3.6????????? concrete wall and a 2x6 frame wall (pony wall) built above the concrete foundation wall. At the time of the assessment, the pony wall insulation was R-19. The pony wall insulation level is not enough and does not meet the actual city standard of R-28. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standards.</foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the wood windows by Energy Star certified units.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
